 "card_notes": [
  {
   "text": "- Context Length: 262,144 natively and extensible up to 1,010,000 tokens.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L64"
  },
  {
   "text": "> Qwen3.5 models operate in thinking mode by default, generating thinking content signified by `<think>\\n...</think>\\n\\n` before producing the final responses.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L712"
  },
  {
   "text": "> To disable thinking content and obtain direct response, refer to the examples [here](#instruct-or-non-thinking-mode).",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L713"
  },
  {
   "text": "> The model has a default context length of 262,144 tokens.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L730"
  },
  {
   "text": "> However, because Qwen3.5 leverages extended context for complex tasks, we advise maintaining a context length of at least 128K tokens to preserve thinking capabilities.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L732"
  },
  {
   "text": "- **Standard Version**: The following command can be used to create an API endpoint with maximum context length 262,144 tokens using tensor parallel on 8 GPUs.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L745"
  },
  {
   "text": "- **Standard Version**: The following command can be used to create an API endpoint with maximum context length 262,144 tokens using tensor parallel on 8 GPUs.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L776"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Thinking mode for general tasks: `temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L835"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Thinking mode for precise coding tasks (e.g. WebDev): `temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L836"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Instruct (or non-thinking) mode for general tasks: `temperature=0.7, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L837"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Instruct (or non-thinking) mode for reasoning tasks: `temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L838"
  },
  {
   "text": "#### Instruct (or Non-Thinking) Mode",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L954"
  },
  {
   "text": "> Qwen3.5 does not officially support the soft switch of Qwen3, i.e., `/think` and `/nothink`.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L957"
  },
  {
   "text": "> If you are using APIs from Alibaba Cloud Model Studio, in addition to changing `model`, please use `\"enable_thinking\": False` instead of `\"chat_template_kwargs\": {\"enable_thinking\": False}`.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1001"
  },
  {
   "text": "Qwen3.5 natively supports context lengths of up to 262,144 tokens.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1090"
  },
  {
   "text": "For long-horizon tasks where the total length (including both input and output) exceeds this limit, we recommend using RoPE scaling techniques to handle long texts effectively., e.g., YaRN.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1091"
  },
  {
   "text": "YaRN is currently supported by several inference frameworks, e.g., `transformers`, `vllm`, `ktransformers` and `sglang`.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1093"
  },
  {
   "text": "In general, there are two approaches to enabling YaRN for supported frameworks:",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1094"
  },
  {
   "text": "> All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1127"
  },
  {
   "text": "> It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.",
   "source": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B README.md:L1129"
  },
  {
   "text": "- Context Length: 262,144 natively and extensible up to 1,010,000 tokens.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L90"
  },
  {
   "text": "> Qwen3.5 models operate in thinking mode by default, generating thinking content signified by `<think>\\n...</think>\\n\\n` before producing the final responses.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L738"
  },
  {
   "text": "> To disable thinking content and obtain direct response, refer to the examples [here](#instruct-or-non-thinking-mode).",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L739"
  },
  {
   "text": "> The model has a default context length of 262,144 tokens.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L756"
  },
  {
   "text": "> However, because Qwen3.5 leverages extended context for complex tasks, we advise maintaining a context length of at least 128K tokens to preserve thinking capabilities.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L758"
  },
  {
   "text": "- **Standard Version**: The following command can be used to create an API endpoint with maximum context length 262,144 tokens using tensor parallel on 8 GPUs.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L771"
  },
  {
   "text": "- **Standard Version**: The following command can be used to create an API endpoint with maximum context length 262,144 tokens using tensor parallel on 8 GPUs.",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L802"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Thinking mode for general tasks: `temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
   "source": "unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF README.md:L861"
  },
  {
   "text": "> - Thinking mode for precise coding tasks (e.g. WebDev): `temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0`",
